{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114484","id":3139830746,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc67JgPa","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114484","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114484.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114484.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114484","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114484/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114484/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114484/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b815c88decbcbebd2c78fedeb4e103ba8fd2ad5f","number":114484,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Metal: Refactor; fix dynamic uniforms; acyclic render graph support","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n>\r\n> The majority of the **Files Changed** was to add the metal-cpp headers to `thirdparty/metal-cpp`. This is in the first commit, so that it is easier to see the changes specific to Metal. **146 of the changed files are additions to `thirdparty/metal-cpp`.**\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces a major refactoring of the Metal rendering driver with three key improvements:\r\n\r\n### metal-cpp\r\n\r\nRefactors the code to use C++ rather than Objective-C with the following intended benefits:\r\n\r\n- make it more approachable for existing rendering developers\r\n- can use existing Godot containers for Metal objects, which are now C++ structs / classes\r\n- consistent with other RDDs, which are pure C++\r\n- Explicit reference counting, to remove ugly `__unsafe_unretained` and other compiler directives to disable ARC\r\n    - This will provide other advantages, including using [command buffers with unretained references](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/mtlcommandqueue/makecommandbufferwithunretainedreferences()?language=objc) to further reduce CPU overhead. We can do this, because we'll be explicitly tracking resources in the Metal RDD.\r\n- Given explicit memory management (no ARC in C++ code), there are cases where generated code could be quite a bit smaller. See [this gist](https://gist.github.com/stuartcarnie/4af9775529dd091cf5213370b38876b6)\r\n\r\n### Architecture Refactoring\r\n\r\nThe primary purpose of these changes were to separate common code that can be shared with Metal 3 and Metal 4. I have a complete Metal 4 renderer working with this branch to prove the refactoring is complete.\r\n\r\n- **Split Metal objects**: Renamed `metal_objects.h/mm` → `metal3_objects.h/mm` and extracted shared code into new `metal_objects_shared.h/cpp`\r\n- **New MTL3 namespace**: Created dedicated namespace for Metal 3-specific functionality with `MTL3::RenderingDeviceDriverMetal` class\r\n- **Command buffer hierarchy**: `MDCommandBuffer` now inherits from `MDCommandBufferBase` with virtual methods for polymorphic dispatch to Metal 3 and Metal 4 in the future.\r\n- **Cleaner separation**: Shared types (`MDRenderPass`, `MDAttachment`, `MDSubpass`, `MDFrameBuffer`, shaders, pipelines) moved to shared header for reuse\r\n- **Methods refactored**: `bind_uniforms_argument_buffers` moved from `MDUniformSet` to `MDCommandBuffer`, which is Metal 3 specific\r\n\r\n### Dynamic Uniforms Fix\r\n\r\nA hack was implemented to disable argument buffers (and use slot binding) when a shader used dynamic uniforms. This has been resolved with this update.\r\n\r\n- **Ring buffer allocation**: Added `MDRingBuffer` class for efficient transient GPU memory allocations (16-byte aligned, 64KB default segments)\r\n- **GPU address-based binding**: Dynamic uniform buffers now use `MTLGPUAddress` for argument buffer updates instead of per-frame buffer copies using slot binding, which was a hack.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Acyclic Render Graph Support\r\n\r\nMoving to ARG should provide an overall performance gain, especially when there are a large number of resources (textures and buffers) in use. Overall CPU usage is expected to be lower when ARG is used.\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n>\r\n> ARG is opt-in. Specify `GODOT_MTL_FORCE_BARRIERS=1` to enable the ARG. Eventually it will be available as a project setting.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional Changes\r\n\r\n- **MetalFX updates**: Fixes a TODO to handle resource lifetime of scaler objects generically to allow for Metal 4 support in the future.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279